  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Xenon undergo $s p^3$ hybridization.\n<img src=\"assets\\st0160_f02fa587d41b.png\"><br>\nIn the fourth excited state xenon atom, has 8 unpaired electrons<img src=\"assets\\st0160_5d30588779d0.png\"><br>\nOne $s$ and three $p$ orbital undergo $s p^3$ hybridization. Four $s p^3$ hybrid orbitals form four $\\sigma$ bonds with oxygen atoms. They are $\\sigma s p^3-p$. Four $p \\pi-d \\pi$ bonds are also formed with oxygen atoms by the unpaired electrons."
